# Files that must never ship in the published tarball.
#
# The `files` allowlist in package.json already covers the intended surface,
# but npm still packs some dot-entries and generated artifacts that live under
# an allowlisted directory. .archlint-cache/ is archlint's own cache: it is
# regenerated on every run, it grows without bound, and its two files
# (git-history.redb, cache.bin) accounted for 2.16 MB of a 2.88 MB tarball —
# enough to trip the 2 MB size guard in Cross-Platform CI.
.archlint-cache/
*.redb
*.bin

# Editor and OS scratch files.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Tests ship with the package only by accident: nothing under bin/, hooks/ or the
# runtime libraries imports them, and measured they are the largest single block --
# lib/__tests__ alone is 1.47 MB of a 2.27 MB tarball, which is what pushed it past the
# 2 MB guard. Excluding them is not a size trick: a test file is not a thing the package

# Test files are not shipped. Nothing under bin/, hooks/ or the runtime libraries
# imports them, and measurably lib/__tests__ alone is 1.47 MB of the tarball -- it is what
# made the package cross the 2 MB guard.  is used rather than a negative
# entry in  because the package's own contract forbids __tests__ in 
# (scripts/__tests__/gates-shipped.test.cjs), and an .npmignore pattern subtracts from
# an allowlisted directory without touching that list.
lib/__tests__/
gates/__tests__/
principles/**/__tests__/
mutation/**/__tests__/
mock-policy/**/__tests__/
build-integrity/**/__tests__/
plugins/**/__tests__/
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.mjs
